Z||000000||86_Fastback||08-24-2000||03:20 PM||||I am starting to iron out the details for a 3.4l swap in my 86  GT.   My questions involve the intake manifold.   I am not to concerned about stealth, but everyone mentions using the fiero's.  Which one would give better performance?  Disadvantages/advantages for both?  <BR><P>------------------<BR> ||||reg||5
Z||000001||Alex4mula||08-24-2000||03:33 PM||||Fiero one should flow OK up to 200HP. Maybe more. Also could be ported. Main problem I have heard is obstruction to the distributor from others.||||reg||1
Z||000002||lou_dias||08-25-2000||12:25 PM||||I'd recommend doing the full swap from a minivan or grand am GT.  Then new GT's even come with an updated Getrag 5 speed that even syncronizes reverse gear.  ACE Engine conversions can get you a wiring harness I think...  You get more power with SFI and especially the aluminum heads.  You may just want to pull the valve covers off and add 1.6 roller rockers and some porting.||||reg||1
